Description: Tell one trusted client which window the person points at, and show it
 Adds zyantrik_window_locator_v1, a private protocol offered only to the one
 client labwc launches itself on a pre-connected socket from
 <yantrik locator="/absolute/program" private="app ids"> (launch-client.c),
 and again as soon as it exits (at most every 5 s).
 .
 labwc starts it only when every rc.xml it read was root's and writable by no
 one else, in a folder that is too (checked on each file as rcxml_read opened
 it), the private list names at least one app id, and the command is one
 absolute path, with no arguments, to a program that is root's alone in a
 folder that is too (re-checked at every launch). The command and the list are
 taken once, when labwc starts. The client runs with a short list of
 environment variables, not labwc's whole environment, and its connection is
 not offered the virtual input, input method, foreign toplevel, screencopy,
 dmabuf export, data control or session lock protocols.
 .
 The person's gesture is checked here: `at` is answered with a window only
 while a pointer button pressed on the client's own surface is held at the
 cursor (the drag that began on its mark), and `focused` only within 2 s
 after the new YantrikLocate action (Super+Y), once. A picture, rendered
 offscreen from that window's own scene subtree (scene-capture.c) into a
 sealed memory file, needs a fresh answer: only the window the most recent
 answer named, within 2 s, once, and for an `at` answer only after the button
 is released (the drop). Windows on the private list are named without a
 title and never pictured; windows off the current workspace are never named.
 Every picture, and every refused picture of a private window, is logged. At
 most 120 answers and 2 pictures a second; nothing while the session is
 locked. The point lookup looks through the client's own surfaces (its drag
 overlay) and stops at anyone else's.
 .
 Other clients can still synthesize both gestures with virtual input: this
 holds the launched client to the person's action, and is not a boundary
 against programs running as the person (yantrikos/yantrik-os#414, #476). It
 also assumes labwc itself was started from root's files (yantrik-session).
 Built for Yantrik OS's Y Anywhere (design/y-anywhere-2026-11-22.md).
Author: Yantrik OS <dev@yantrikos.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
